      "description": "Watch Inter vs Monza highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 22, 2026. Inter Milan and Monza locked horns at the San Siro in a clash that promised tactical intrigue and high-intensity football from the opening whistle. The encounter on August 22, 2026, saw both teams testing each other's resolve in a classic Italian top-flight atmosphere. Early Fireworks and a Quick Response The match ignited early for the home side. In just the 6th minute, Inter took the lead when Hakan Calhanoglu unleashed a powerful strike from outside the box, finding the net after being set up by Andy Diouf . A VAR check followed, but the goal stood, sending the home crowd into raptures. However, Monza refused to be intimidated by the early deficit. They grew into the game and found an equalizer in the 29th minute. Gustavo Varela clinical finish with his right foot, assisted by Mathis Mout , restored parity and set the stage for a competitive battle through the remainder of the first half. Inter Take Charge in the Second Half The second half saw Inter shift into a higher gear, asserting their dominance almost immediately after the restart. In the 48th minute, Piotr Zielinski reacted quickest to a loose ball in the area, firing home to put the Nerazzurri back in front. The momentum stayed firmly with the hosts, and in the 55th minute, Francesco Pio Esposito produced a moment of individual brilliance, scoring with a fantastic back-heel following a cross from Andy Diouf . The clinical nature of the performance continued as Yann Aurel Bisseck added a fourth in the 63rd minute, finishing with his left foot after a key pass from Esposito . Dominance and Closing Stages With a comfortable lead established, Inter controlled the tempo, finishing the match with an overwhelming 71% possession. Tactical substitutions followed, with John Stones and Aleksandar Stankovic coming on to see out the result. Monza struggled to find a way back into the contest, hindered by several offside calls and a yellow card for Lorenzo Lucchesi late in the game for a tactical foul. Despite a few late attempts at goal from the home side, the scoreline remained unchanged until the final whistle, confirming a comprehensive victory for the Milan giants in front of their home supporters."
